US-001 is done. Summary of what I implemented:

## Changes

**New: `frontend/src/utils/logger.js`**
Exports a default `{ debug, info, warn, error }` object. `debug` and `info` bail out when `process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production'`; `warn` and `error` always delegate to `console`. The env check runs per call rather than at module load, so CRA's build-time inlining still folds the branch in production while tests can toggle `NODE_ENV` without `jest.resetModules()`.

**New: `frontend/src/utils/__tests__/logger.test.js`**
8 tests covering all four levels in both `production` and `development` — including the required assertion that `debug` does not call `console.log` in production and does in development.

**Replaced 88 `console.*` calls across 29 files** (`core/`, `context/`, `components/`, `pages/`, `pages/administration/`): 84 `console.error` → `logger.error`, 4 `console.log` → `logger.debug`, 1 `console.warn` → `logger.warn`. The `import logger from ".../utils/logger"` line was inserted after each file's last import, matching that file's quote style (single quotes in `core/*.js`, double elsewhere). The stale CRA comment in `index.js` (`reportWebVitals(console.log)`) was reworded to `logger.debug` so the acceptance grep is clean.

